      "evidence": "The cited `thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-bounded-fixed-n-operator` defines the Fourier convention as “\\(\\widehat f(\\xi)=\\int f(X)e^{-2\\pi iX\\cdot\\xi}\\,dX\\)” and its kinetic multiplier as “\\(\\kappa(\\xi)=\\sum_i\\frac{\\hbar^2}{2m_i}|\\xi_i|^2\\)”. For the standard Euclidean Laplacian, this makes the corresponding differential operator \\(-\\sum_i\\hbar^2\\Delta_i/(8\\pi^2m_i)\\). Fact [F4] instead identifies the equal-mass operator with \\(-\\sum_i\\hbar^2\\Delta_i/(2m)\\), off by a factor of \\(4\\pi^2\\).",
